KNOWNBUG
disable_iff2.sv
--bound 3
^\[main\.assume\.1\] always \(main\.a \|=> main\.rst\): ASSUMED$
^\[main\.p0\] always \(disable iff \(main\.rst\) main\.a \|=> main\.b\): PROVED up to bound 3$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The disable condition is only evaluated at the start of the evaluation
attempt: rewrite_disable_iff (src/temporal-logic/normalize_property.cpp)
turns "disable iff (rst) p" into "rst || p", where rst is a state
predicate evaluated in the first cycle of the attempt.  Per 1800-2017
16.12, the attempt is disabled if rst becomes true at any cycle during
the evaluation of p.  EBMC reports REFUTED.
